<!-- l4: decide:a WA person, in full -->

**100.** In relation to a STRING “the person’s name”, a STRING “the reference”, an optional DATE “when the person was born”, a Vital status “whether the person is living”, a list of Child “the person’s children”, a BOOLEAN “in actual military service”, a BOOLEAN “at sea” and a BOOLEAN “so circumstanced”, a WA person, in full means Person where name is the person’s name, the reference for this person is the reference, date of birth is when the person was born, vital status is whether the person is living, children is the person’s children, at the date of the death only conceived in the womb but subsequently born alive is FALSE, money or other property given, paid or settled by the intestate during his life to or for the advancement of the person is 0, the date on which the person attains the age of majority is NOTHING, a soldier being in actual military service is in actual military service, a mariner or seaman being at sea is at sea, a member of any naval or marine forces so circumstanced that if he were a soldier he would be in actual military service is so circumstanced, so desires that letters of administration be granted to such person as the court thinks fit is FALSE, lacks mental capacity (within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act 2008) to make decisions with respect to the management and administration of the person's property and affairs is FALSE, absent from Singapore is FALSE and willing to act is TRUE.

