<!-- l4: decide:the facts about a will, in full -->

**133.** In relation to a Will “the instrument”, a The position of the signature “where the signature is”, a Conformity of the execution of a will to a law outside this Act “the conformity facts”, a The ways in which a will may have been revoked “the revocation facts”, a The revival of a revoked will “the revival facts”, a BOOLEAN “duly executed counting only the disinterested witnesses”, a BOOLEAN “a subsequent conveyance or other act”, a BOOLEAN “that conveyance being the act by which the will is revoked”, a BOOLEAN “a contrary intention as to the time from which it speaks”, a BOOLEAN “a contrary intention as to lapse” and a BOOLEAN “it would have been valid as an informal disposition of personal estate”, the facts about a will, in full means A will, with the facts about it that only this Act asks where the will is the instrument, the position of the signature is where the signature is, the conformity of its execution to a law outside this Act is the conformity facts, the ways in which it has been revoked is the revocation facts, its revival is the revival facts, the signature was made or acknowledged by the testator as the signature to his will or codicil in the presence of 2 or more witnesses present at the same time, counting only witnesses to whom and to whose wife or husband no such disposition is given or made is duly executed counting only the disinterested witnesses, a conveyance or other act has been made or done subsequently to its execution, of or relating to any real or personal estate therein comprised is a subsequent conveyance or other act, that conveyance or other act is an act by which the will is revoked as aforesaid is that conveyance being the act by which the will is revoked, a contrary intention appears by the will as to the time from which it speaks is a contrary intention as to the time from which it speaks, a contrary intention appears by the will as to the lapse of a devise or bequest to a child or other issue is a contrary intention as to lapse and made in such manner and form that if the disposition had been a disposition of personal estate made by that person it would have been valid is it would have been valid as an informal disposition of personal estate.

<!-- l4: decide:the facts about a will -->

**134.** In relation to a Will “the instrument”, a Conformity of the execution of a will to a law outside this Act “the conformity facts”, a The ways in which a will may have been revoked “the revocation facts”, a The revival of a revoked will “the revival facts”, a BOOLEAN “duly executed counting only the disinterested witnesses”, a BOOLEAN “a subsequent conveyance or other act”, a BOOLEAN “a contrary intention as to the time from which it speaks”, a BOOLEAN “a contrary intention as to lapse” and a BOOLEAN “it would have been valid as an informal disposition of personal estate”, the facts about a will means the facts about a will, in full with the instrument, the signature placed so that with there is a signature, there is a signature, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE, the conformity facts, the revocation facts, the revival facts, duly executed counting only the disinterested witnesses, a subsequent conveyance or other act, FALSE, a contrary intention as to the time from which it speaks, a contrary intention as to lapse and it would have been valid as an informal disposition of personal estate.

For the purposes of this provision—

“there is a signature” means the instrument's signed at the foot or end thereof by the testator or the instrument's signed at the foot or end thereof by some other person in his presence and by his direction;

<!-- l4: decide:the plain facts about -->

**135.** In relation to a Will “the instrument”, the plain facts about means the facts about a will with the instrument, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a WA grant -->

**136.** In relation to a Kind of grant “what kind”, an optional DATE “the date”, a Limitation on the grant “the limitation of the grant”, a BOOLEAN “it was sealed under section 47(1)” and an optional DATE “the date it was sealed”, a WA grant means Grant where the kind of grant is what kind, the grantees is EMPTY, the date of the grant is the date, the limitation is the limitation of the grant, the court that made the grant is a court within the meaning of these Acts with the General Division of the High Court, the exception subject to which the grant is made is NOTHING, expired by effluxion of time or by the happening of the event or contingency on which it was limited is FALSE, revoked is FALSE, has given such security as is lawfully required to be furnished is TRUE, has been extracted is TRUE, sealed under section 47(1) of the Probate and Administration Act 1934 is it was sealed under section 47(1) and the date of the sealing is the date it was sealed.

<!-- l4: decide:a WA infant concerned in the estate -->

**137.** In relation to a Person “the infant child”, an optional Person “the father of the child” and a list of Guardian “the guardians”, a WA infant concerned in the estate means Infant where the infant is the infant child, the father of the infant is the father of the child, the mother of the infant is NOTHING, the guardians of the infant is the guardians, some other person has parental rights with respect to him is FALSE, the income of the property of the infant is 0, the capital of the property of the infant is 0 and of an age to express an independent opinion is FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a WA deceased person, with the infants concerned in the estate -->

**138.** In relation to a Person “the person who died”, a Family “the family of the deceased”, an optional Will “the will of the deceased”, a list of Grant “the grants” and a list of Infant “the infants”, a WA deceased person, with the infants concerned in the estate means Deceased person where the deceased is the person who died, the family is the family of the deceased, the estate is an estate of no recorded value, the will is the will of the deceased, domiciled in Singapore at the time of his death is TRUE, carried on business or resided in Singapore within 12 months of his death is TRUE, a Muslim is FALSE, the grants made in respect of the estate is the grants, the probate applications made in respect of the estate is EMPTY, a next of kin, creditor or other person has appeared and made out a claim to letters of administration is FALSE and the infants concerned in the estate is the infants.

<!-- l4: decide:a WA deceased person -->

**139.** In relation to a Person “the person who died”, a Family “the family of the deceased”, an optional Will “the will of the deceased” and a list of Grant “the grants”, a WA deceased person means a WA deceased person, with the infants concerned in the estate with the person who died, the family of the deceased, the will of the deceased, the grants and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:a case -->

**140.** In relation to a Deceased person “the deceased person”, an A will, with the facts about it that only this Act asks “the will and its further facts”, a BOOLEAN “an application has been made”, an optional DATE “the date of the application”, a BOOLEAN “permission has been given” and a BOOLEAN “a grant of the remainder”, a case means A case under this Act where the deceased is the deceased person, the will in question is the will and its further facts, an application for an order under section 28(1) has been made is an application has been made, the date of that application is the date of the application, a court has given permission for the application to be made after the end of that period is permission has been given and a grant limited to the remainder of the testator’s estate has previously been made or is made at the same time is a grant of the remainder.

