**226.** In relation to a Person “the maker of the will”, an ordinary will made by means a will with the maker of the will, JUST with YMD with 1985, 3 and 1, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, list of Devi attesting and taking a legacy, Bala attesting and Chandra attesting, list of a pecuniary legacy of $10,000 to Devi, EMPTY, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the will of Zubaida, devising to the reference two of her children share -->

**227.** The will of Zubaida, devising to the reference two of her children share means a will with the WA Zubaida, JUST with YMD with 2015, 3 and 1, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, list of Bala attesting and Chandra attesting, list of a specific devise to the reference Yasmin and Zainab share, EMPTY, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a plain case -->

**228.** In relation to a Person “the person who died”, a Family “the family of the deceased” and a Will “the instrument”, a plain case means a case with a WA deceased person with the person who died, the family of the deceased, JUST with the instrument and EMPTY, the plain facts about with the instrument, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:a case with -->

**229.** In relation to a Person “the person who died”, a Family “the family of the deceased”, an A will, with the facts about it that only this Act asks “the will and its further facts” and a list of Grant “the grants”, a case with means a case with a WA deceased person with the person who died, the family of the deceased, JUST with the will and its further facts's the will and the grants, the will and its further facts, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE and FALSE.

## Worked facts — the alterations, the signature positions and the grants

<!-- l4: decide:an alteration -->

**230.** In relation to a BOOLEAN “the earlier words are apparent”, a BOOLEAN “it is executed in the like manner”, a BOOLEAN “signed in the margin” and a BOOLEAN “signed opposite a memorandum”, an alteration means An alteration made in a will after its execution where the words or effect of the will before the alteration are apparent is the earlier words are apparent, the alteration is executed in the like manner as by this Act is required for the execution of the will is it is executed in the like manner, the signature of the testator and the subscription of the witnesses are made in the margin or on some other part of the will opposite or near to the alteration is signed in the margin and the signature of the testator and the subscription of the witnesses are made at the foot or end of or opposite to a memorandum referring to the alteration and written at the end or some other part of the will is signed opposite a memorandum.

<!-- l4: decide:an obliteration that leaves the earlier words legible, unattested -->

**231.** An obliteration that leaves the earlier words legible, unattested means an alteration with TRUE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an obliteration that leaves the earlier words illegible, unattested -->

**232.** An obliteration that leaves the earlier words illegible, unattested means an alteration with FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an interlineation, the earlier words legible, signed in the margin -->

**233.** An interlineation, the earlier words legible, signed in the margin means an alteration with TRUE, FALSE, TRUE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an interlineation, the earlier words legible, signed opposite a memorandum -->

**234.** An interlineation, the earlier words legible, signed opposite a memorandum means an alteration with TRUE, FALSE, FALSE and TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:an interlineation, the earlier words legible, executed in the like manner as the will -->

**235.** An interlineation, the earlier words legible, executed in the like manner as the will means an alteration with TRUE, TRUE, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the devise to Ismail -->

**236.** In relation to a STRING “where it stands”, the devise to Ismail means A disposition, and where it stands in relation to the signature where the disposition is a specific devise to Ismail, underneath or following the signature is where it stands is equal to below the signature and inserted after the signature was made is where it stands is equal to inserted after the signature was made.

<!-- l4: decide:the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020 -->

**237.** The grant of probate made on 1 March 2020 means a WA grant with probate, JUST with YMD with 2020, 3 and 1, not limited, FALSE and NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:the grant of probate made on 31 August 2020 -->

**238.** The grant of probate made on 31 August 2020 means a WA grant with probate, JUST with YMD with 2020, 8 and 31, not limited, FALSE and NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:a grant of probate whose date is not in evidence -->

**239.** A grant of probate whose date is not in evidence means a WA grant with probate, NOTHING, not limited, FALSE and NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:the grant limited to settled land made on 1 February 2020 -->

**240.** The grant limited to settled land made on 1 February 2020 means a WA grant with letters of administration with the will annexed, JUST with YMD with 2020, 2 and 1, limited to settled land or to trust property, FALSE and NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:the grant limited to a part of the estate made on 1 February 2020 -->

**241.** The grant limited to a part of the estate made on 1 February 2020 means a WA grant with letters of administration with the will annexed, JUST with YMD with 2020, 2 and 1, limited to a part only of the testator’s estate with the Malaysian assets, FALSE and NOTHING.

<!-- l4: decide:the probate resealed on 1 September 2020, granted on 1 March 2020 -->

**242.** The probate resealed on 1 September 2020, granted on 1 March 2020 means a WA grant with probate, JUST with YMD with 2020, 3 and 1, not limited, TRUE and JUST with YMD with 2020, 9 and 1.

<!-- l4: decide:the letters of administration sealed on 1 September 2020, granted on 1 March 2020 -->

**243.** The letters of administration sealed on 1 September 2020, granted on 1 March 2020 means a WA grant with letters of administration, JUST with YMD with 2020, 3 and 1, not limited, TRUE and JUST with YMD with 2020, 9 and 1.

