**320.** The case of a will destroyed by another person at the testator’s direction, with the intention of revoking it means the case of Amrita’s will, revoked and revived thus with revoked with FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE and TRUE and no revival.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of a will revoked by a later will and then re-executed -->

**321.** The case of a will revoked by a later will and then re-executed means the case of Amrita’s will, revoked and revived thus with revoked with TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE and revived with TRUE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of a will re-executed but never revoked -->

**322.** The case of a will re-executed but never revoked means the case of Amrita’s will, revoked and revived thus with not revoked in any of those ways and revived with TRUE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of a will partly revoked, then wholly revoked, then revived by codicil -->

**323.** The case of a will partly revoked, then wholly revoked, then revived by codicil means the case of Amrita’s will, revoked and revived thus with revoked with TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE and revived with FALSE, TRUE, TRUE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the same will, a contrary intention being shown -->

**324.** The case of the same will, a contrary intention being shown means the case of Amrita’s will, revoked and revived thus with revoked with TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE and revived with FALSE, TRUE, TRUE and TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it -->

**325.** In relation to a Family “the family of the deceased”, a The ways in which a will may have been revoked “the revocation facts” and a BOOLEAN “the conveyance is itself the revoking act”, the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it means a case with with the WA Amrita, the family of the deceased, the facts about a will, in full with the will of Amrita, the signature in an unremarkable position, no conformity to any law outside this Act, the revocation facts, no revival, FALSE, TRUE, the conveyance is itself the revoking act, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of a conveyance made after the will, the will standing -->

**326.** The case of a conveyance made after the will, the will standing means the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it with no marriages, not revoked in any of those ways and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of a conveyance that is itself the act by which the will is revoked -->

**327.** The case of a conveyance that is itself the act by which the will is revoked means the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it with no marriages, revoked with FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE and TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of a conveyance made after the will, the will having been revoked by a marriage -->

**328.** The case of a conveyance made after the will, the will having been revoked by a marriage means the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it with married Gita in 2018, after the will, not revoked in any of those ways and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of a conveyance made after the will, the will having been revoked by a later will -->

**329.** The case of a conveyance made after the will, the will having been revoked by a later will means the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it with no marriages, revoked with TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of a conveyance said to be the revoking act, no mode of revocation in section 15 being made out -->

**330.** The case of a conveyance said to be the revoking act, no mode of revocation in section 15 being made out means the case of Amrita’s will and a conveyance made after it with no marriages, not revoked in any of those ways and TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of a will showing a contrary intention as to the time from which it speaks -->

**331.** The case of a will showing a contrary intention as to the time from which it speaks means a case with with the WA Amrita, no marriages, the facts about a will with the will of Amrita, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE and FALSE and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of a will showing a contrary intention as to lapse -->

**332.** The case of a will showing a contrary intention as to lapse means a case with with the WA Amrita, no marriages, the facts about a will with the will of Amrita, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE and FALSE and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the will of Farid -->

**333.** The case of the will of Farid means a case with with the WA Farid, no marriages, the facts about a will with the will of Farid, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and TRUE and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the will of Osman -->

**334.** The case of the will of Osman means a case with with the WA Osman, no marriages, the facts about a will with the will of Osman, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and TRUE and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the will of Farid, the old form not being made out -->

**335.** The case of the will of Farid, the old form not being made out means a case with with the WA Farid, no marriages, the facts about a will with the will of Farid, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of an informal will made by -->

**336.** In relation to a Person “the privileged testator” and an optional DATE “the date it was written”, the case of an informal will made by means a case with with the privileged testator, no marriages, the facts about a will with a will with the privileged testator, the date it was written, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, EMPTY, EMPTY, list of a guardian appointed by the father by will with the WA Bala and suri, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE and FALSE, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and TRUE and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the informal will of Rashid, a civilian -->

**337.** The case of the informal will of Rashid, a civilian means the case of an informal will made by with the WA Rashid and JUST with YMD with 2023, 2 and 2.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the will of Pak, a mariner at sea -->

**338.** The case of the will of Pak, a mariner at sea means the case of an informal will made by with the WA Pak and JUST with YMD with 2023, 2 and 2.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the will of Quek, a member of the naval forces -->

**339.** The case of the will of Quek, a member of the naval forces means the case of an informal will made by with the WA Quek and JUST with YMD with 2023, 3 and 3.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the will of Wahid, who died on 30 August 1938 -->

**340.** The case of the will of Wahid, who died on 30 August 1938 means the case of an informal will made by with the WA Wahid and JUST with YMD with 1938, 8 and 1.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the will of Farid, appointing no guardian -->

**341.** The case of the will of Farid, appointing no guardian means a case with with the WA Farid, no marriages, the facts about a will with the will of Farid, appointing no guardian, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and TRUE and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the will of Farid, appointing a guardian of a child who is not his -->

**342.** The case of the will of Farid, appointing a guardian of a child who is not his means a case with with the WA Farid, no marriages, the facts about a will with the will of Farid, appointing a guardian of a child who is not his, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and TRUE and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the will of Farid, appointing two guardians, one of them of a child who is not his -->

**343.** The case of the will of Farid, appointing two guardians, one of them of a child who is not his means a case with with the WA Farid, no marriages, the facts about a will with the will of Farid, appointing two guardians, one of them of a child who is not his, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and TRUE and EMPTY.

<!-- l4: decide:the case of the will of Farid, Jaya being an infant concerned in the estate -->

**344.** The case of the will of Farid, Jaya being an infant concerned in the estate means a case with a WA deceased person, with the infants concerned in the estate with the WA Farid, no marriages, JUST with the will of Farid, EMPTY and list of a WA infant concerned in the estate with the WA Jaya, JUST with the WA Farid and list of the guardian Farid appointed of his child Jaya, the facts about a will with the will of Farid, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and TRUE, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:the rectification case -->

**345.** In relation to a list of Grant “the grants”, a BOOLEAN “an application”, an optional DATE “the date of the application”, a BOOLEAN “permission” and a BOOLEAN “a grant of the remainder”, the rectification case means a case with a WA deceased person with the WA Amrita, no marriages, JUST with the will of Amrita and the grants, the facts about a will with the will of Amrita, no conformity to any law outside this Act, not revoked in any of those ways, no revival, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE and FALSE, an application, the date of the application, permission and a grant of the remainder.

<!-- l4: decide:no application to rectify has been made -->

**346.** No application to rectify has been made means the rectification case with list of the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020, FALSE, NOTHING, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify made 5 months after the grant -->

**347.** An application to rectify made 5 months after the grant means the rectification case with list of the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2020, 8 and 1, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify made 8 months after the grant -->

**348.** An application to rectify made 8 months after the grant means the rectification case with list of the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2020, 11 and 1, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify made 8 months after the grant, with the permission of a court -->

**349.** An application to rectify made 8 months after the grant, with the permission of a court means the rectification case with list of the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2020, 11 and 1, TRUE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify, no grant having been made -->

**350.** An application to rectify, no grant having been made means the rectification case with EMPTY, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2020, 8 and 1, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify, only a grant limited to settled land having been made -->

**351.** An application to rectify, only a grant limited to settled land having been made means the rectification case with list of the grant limited to settled land made on 1 February 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2020, 11 and 1, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify, only a grant limited to part of the estate having been made -->

**352.** An application to rectify, only a grant limited to part of the estate having been made means the rectification case with list of the grant limited to a part of the estate made on 1 February 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2020, 11 and 1, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify, a grant of the remainder having also been made -->

**353.** An application to rectify, a grant of the remainder having also been made means the rectification case with list of the grant limited to a part of the estate made on 1 February 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2020, 11 and 1, FALSE and TRUE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify made 10 months after a probate that was resealed -->

**354.** An application to rectify made 10 months after a probate that was resealed means the rectification case with list of the probate resealed on 1 September 2020, granted on 1 March 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2021, 1 and 1, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify made 10 months after letters of administration that were sealed -->

**355.** An application to rectify made 10 months after letters of administration that were sealed means the rectification case with list of the letters of administration sealed on 1 September 2020, granted on 1 March 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2021, 1 and 1, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify whose date is not in evidence -->

**356.** An application to rectify whose date is not in evidence means the rectification case with list of the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020, TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify made on the last day of the 6 months -->

**357.** An application to rectify made on the last day of the 6 months means the rectification case with list of the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2020, 9 and 1, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify made one day after the 6 months -->

**358.** An application to rectify made one day after the 6 months means the rectification case with list of the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2020, 9 and 2, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify made on 28 February 2021, the grant being on 31 August 2020 -->

**359.** An application to rectify made on 28 February 2021, the grant being on 31 August 2020 means the rectification case with list of the grant of probate made on 31 August 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2021, 2 and 28, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify made on 1 March 2021, the grant being on 31 August 2020 -->

**360.** An application to rectify made on 1 March 2021, the grant being on 31 August 2020 means the rectification case with list of the grant of probate made on 31 August 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2021, 3 and 1, FALSE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify whose date is not in evidence, made with the permission of a court -->

**361.** An application to rectify whose date is not in evidence, made with the permission of a court means the rectification case with list of the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020, TRUE, NOTHING, TRUE and FALSE.

<!-- l4: decide:an application to rectify, one of the two grants being undated -->

**362.** An application to rectify, one of the two grants being undated means the rectification case with list of a grant of probate whose date is not in evidence and the grant of probate made on 1 March 2020, TRUE, JUST with YMD with 2020, 8 and 1, FALSE and FALSE.

